Seam: RegisterLocalState and RegisterProfilePrefs in
      chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc, among the calls that ask each
      subsystem to register the settings it owns, and the deps that let that
      file see them.
Why: how updates are allowed to arrive is one setting for the installation
     rather than one per profile -- there is one application on disk and
     every profile runs from it -- and local state is where Chromium keeps
     settings of that kind. A profile's startup behaviour is its own setting,
     and Arcium's default differs from Chromium's: a Today tab lives only in
     the session, so a profile that opens a new tab page at launch loses all
     of them at every quit. The same call registers the welcome's progress,
     the one profile setting Arcium adds. The profile call sits last so every
     setting it changes the default of is already registered.
Delegates to: arcium::RegisterUpdatePrefs, arcium::SetProfileDefaults
